  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a parallel plate capacitor set up, the plate area of capacitor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and the plates are separated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the space between the plates are filled with a dielectric material of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> (see figure) the capacitance of the set-up will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;________.</p><p>(Dielectric constant of the material <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math>)</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cb8d191b-5036-462a-8fa3-0f3f29babb7e-image.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 229px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The given system can be considered as a series combination of two capacitors. The equivalent capacitance can be given as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p>",
